              <p style="margin-bottom: 0;font-size:18px"">
                Ryan received his PhD from UC Berkeley working on dark matter searches with xenon time projection chambers. 
                Before then, he did undergrad at the University of New Mexico, working on xenon-doped liquid argon detectors for neutrinoless double beta decay experiments. 
